I"<p>Through the <a href="https://nes-lter.whoi.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Northeast U.S. Shelf Long-Term Ecological Research (NES-LTER) program</a>, we study spatial, seasonal, and interannual variability in phytoplankton biomass and community composition. Metacommunity analyses help show when local communities change together and when species composition becomes less synchronized. We also use topic-modeling approaches to identify recurring assemblages within complex image-based plankton datasets.</p>
